data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 480, "run_id": "run_cd4c0444c4ea40cc", "data": {"id": "17a3b07a-72cf-4f5d-887d-edb85b8d7275", "run_id": "run_cd4c0444c4ea40cc", "kind": "tool", "position": 473, "revision": 480, "parent_tool_use_id": "call_cd7d4a0a42064016ac6f0d30", "agent_call_id": "157b379d-b0ad-4072-a333-319334eb7f76", "data": {"name": "Bash", "input": "{\"command\": \"python3 independent_analysis.py 2>&1\", \"description\": \"Run the independent analysis script\", \"timeout\": 300000}", "output": "Exit code 1\n[workspace] RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in power\n  y_pred_pow_t = a_pow_t * buffer_t**b_pow_t\n[workspace] RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in power\n  y_pred_pow_w = a_pow_w * buffer_w**b_pow_w\n============================================================\nFINDING 1: V vs B relationship\n============================================================\n\nMeanfield full linear fit:\n  slope=-0.370571, intercept=2.438115, R²=0.705672, p=7.98e-11\n\nMeanfield segmented regression:\n  breakpoint_Bc=3.55\n  segment1: slope=-0.999862, intercept=3.672669\n  segment2: slope=-0.000004, intercept=0.000032\n  segmented R²=0.999998\n\nTheory (non-zero) linear fit:\n  slope=-1.000000, intercept=3.994308, R²=1.000000, p=0.00e+00\n\nTheory segmented regression:\n  breakpoint_Bc=2.00\n  segment1: slope=-1.000000, intercept=3.994308\n  segment2: slope=-1.000000, intercept=3.994308\n  segmented R²=1.000000\n\n============================================================\nFINDING 2: Correlation collapse\n============================================================\n  ave_1: 2111 points, lag range [0, 42181], corr range [0.0067, 1.0000]\n  ave_2: 1529 points, lag range [0, 15271], corr range [0.0076, 1.0000]\n  ave_3: 1394 points, lag range [0, 5569], corr range [0.0088, 1.0000]\n  ave_4: 825 points, lag range [0, 2470], corr range [0.0072, 1.0000]\n  ave_5: 577 points, lag range [0, 1151], corr range [0.0074, 1.0000]\n  ave_2 vs ave_1: optimal_scale=0.5000, max_correlation=0.993515\n  ave_3 vs ave_1: optimal_scale=0.5000, max_correlation=0.948018\n  ave_4 vs ave_1: optimal_scale=0.5000, max_correlation=0.904806\n  ave_5 vs ave_1: optimal_scale=0.5000, max_correlation=0.876237\n  ave_1 vs ave_2: scale=0.5000, corr=0.993515\n  ave_1 vs ave_3: scale=0.5000, corr=0.948018\n  ave_1 vs ave_4: scale=0.5000, corr=0.904806\n  ave_1 vs ave_5: scale=0.5000, corr=0.876237\n  ave_2 vs ave_3: scale=0.5000, corr=0.997221\n  ave_2 vs ave_4: scale=0.5000, corr=0.955929\n  ave_2 vs ave_5: scale=0.5000, corr=0.913660\n  ave_3 vs ave_4: scale=0.5000, corr=0.998900\n  ave_3 vs ave_5: scale=0.5000, corr=0.964225\n  ave_4 vs ave_5: scale=0.5000, corr=0.999724\n\n============================================================\nFINDING 3: Finite-size scaling\n============================================================\nN_values: [20. 30. 40. 50. 60.] ... (31 points)\nmeanfield_Bc: [2.72390351 2.86481944 2.94397333 3.00192899 3.05339423] ... (31 points)\ntempnet_Bc: [2.824856   2.9370386  3.01297377 3.0643675  3.10445618] ... (31 points)\n\nMeanfield FSS:\n  best nu = 3.2387\n  Bc_inf = 3.836928\n  a = -2.785947\n  R² = 0.999827\n\nTempnet FSS:\n  best nu = 3.4910\n  Bc_inf = 3.858243\n  a = -2.434159\n  R² = 0.999894\n\nMeanfield power-law fit: Bc_inf=3.836704, a=-2.787175, alpha=0.308941, R²=0.999827\nTempnet power-law fit: Bc_inf=3.858291, a=-2.433962, alpha=0.286416, R²=0.999894\n\n============================================================\nFINDING 4: Real-network validation\n============================================================\n\nThiers13:\n  Linear: slope=-0.035267, intercept=0.086108, R²=0.876711, p=9.43e-26\n  Power-law: a=0.005479, b=-3.627987, R²=-inf, p=8.50e-11\n\nWorkplace15:\n  Linear: slope=-0.032561, intercept=0.067427, R²=0.647380, p=1.95e-15\n  Power-law: a=0.002973, b=-3.768762, R²=-inf, p=1.53e-19\n\nResults saved to [workspace]\n\n============================================================\nCOMPARISON WITH ORIGINAL RESULTS\n============================================================\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"[workspace]\", line 485, in <module>\n    orig_mf = original.get(\"meanfield\", {}).get(\"linear_fit\", {})\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: 'list' object has no attribute 'get'", "status": "failed", "is_async": false, "tool_use_id": "call_3ec722f36e5b4a33934461c4"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:19:25.972409+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:19:30.148765+00:00"}}

